  "content": {
    "title": "Rory McIlroy wins Masters, capturing his second green jacket in a row",
    "text": "PGARory McIlroy wins Masters for second straight year, by one strokeMcIlroy rallies from two shots behind and holds off charges by Scottie Scheffler and Justin Rose Garry SmitsJacksonville Florida Times-UnionUpdated April 12, 2026, 7:04 p.m. ETAUGUSTA, Ga. | Rory McIlroy battled back for the second year in a row to win his second Masters Tournament in a row on a hazy and unseasonably hot day on April 12 at the Augusta National Golf Club.McIlroy didn't need to go to a playoff as in 2025 but it was still hard work all the same, as he rallied from two strokes behind Cameron Young through six holes, then held off charges by first Justin Rose and then two-time Masters winner Scottie Scheffler to finish with a 71 and a 72-hole total of 12-under-par 276, one shot clear of Scheffler (68) and two over playing partner Young (73), Rose (70), Tyrrell Hatton (66) and Russell Henley (68).",
